{
  "presses": ["L-middle-home", "R-index-home", "R-index-bottom", "L-pinky-bottom"],
  "locks": {"R-index-bottom": "P"},
  "note": "T3: chord {L-index-home,L-middle-home,R-index-home,R-index-bottom} held {K,O,P,U}. From T2 chord {L-index-home,L-middle-home,R-index-home,R-middle-home}={F,K,O,U} => shared 3 keys {L-index-home,L-middle-home,R-index-home}={K,O,U}; thus new letter P belongs to R-index-bottom. T3 rotation keys {L-index-home,L-pinky-bottom,R-index-top} => R-index-bottom not rotated, so at T4 start R-index-bottom=P. Also L-middle-home,R-index-home not rotated in T3 => each ∈{K,O,U}. Plan T4 press with {R-index-bottom, L-middle-home, R-index-home, L-pinky-bottom} to get multiset including P and determine which letters are on L-middle-home & R-index-home; use next chord to include R-index-top."
}

{
  "presses": ["R-index-home", "R-middle-home", "L-index-home", "L-pinky-top"],
  "note": "T7 ded: L-index-home=I (not rotated). Rot (after T7) included L-pinky-bottom & R-index-home; with only 2 keys, they swap => R-index-home=K now; L-pinky-bottom becomes unknown. Still known pre-rot: R-middle-home=J, R-index-bottom=P. Plan T8: press {R-index-home, R-middle-home, L-index-home, Y=L-pinky-top}; returned set {I,J,K,?} => ded Y letter."
}

{
  "presses": ["L-index-top-in", "L-index-home", "L-middle-home", "R-middle-home"],
  "note": "Resolved from turn13 set {C,E,I,M}: L-index-home=I; L-middle-home=C; L-ring-home=M; L-index-top-in=E. Earlier swap {L-index-top-in,R-index-home-in}={E,F} => R-index-home-in=F. Known: L-index-top-in=E, L-index-home=I, L-middle-home=C, L-ring-home=M, R-ring-home=G, R-index-home-in=F. Next: chord [L-index-top-in,L-index-home,L-middle-home,R-middle-home] to read R-middle-home."
}
